edge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$45$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498778} {:answer/id #uuid "28e2d922-05ab-5c87-9a89-308a6939325d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498818} {:answer/id #uuid "6f1d3fdf-f980-58fa-80aa-e838556de0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$55$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498975} {:answer/id #uuid "70bfdf23-c8f9-5e45-8fc4-8dcadc5bacc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498982} {:answer/id #uuid "b9eef285-487b-5f19-85cc-02493471b540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$60$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$45$ roses" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498778} :answer-field/id #uuid "2915fff9-a5b4-5d3f-b71d-57e7e6ac1978" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e57d984e-c871-52fc-b8d7-34ff3957d67c" :question/math-academy-id "q-60067" :question/problem "The number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden is shown in the following table:\n\n| Roses | Orchids |\n| --- | --- |\n| $33$ | $18$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn Serena's garden, there are approximately $30$ orchids. The ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids is equal in both gardens. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of roses in Serena's garden." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden:\n\n- Roses: $33⟶30$\n\n- Orchids: $18⟶20$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{20}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of roses and the denominator represents the number of orchids.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30÷10}{20÷10}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $15$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 15}{2\\times 15}=\\frac{45}{30}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $45$ roses in Serena's garden."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1acabbdc-ca40-5169-86fa-94633dbacba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498788} {:answer/id #uuid "2c00f90c-1fb9-5090-9bb2-9a477735cada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498825} {:answer/id #uuid "d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499196} {:answer/id #uuid "d6112a9b-d3bc-512d-aa34-95b96d7cf8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499209} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3b4d3f-4f3a-56fd-b4da-2c25a2897600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ cats" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499196} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbb387d-7a25-5bb2-8ab3-ac3326b883b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2ff2ee0-f6fe-5976-b859-e0adc12b8590" :question/math-academy-id "q-60069" :question/problem "The number of dogs and cats in shelter A is shown in the following table:\n\n| Dogs | Cats |\n| --- | --- |\n| $51$ | $32$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn shelter B there are approximately $20$ dogs. The ratio of the number of dogs to the number of cats in both shelters is the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of cats in shelter B." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of dogs and cats in shelter A:\n\n- Dogs: $51⟶50$\n\n- Cats: $32⟶30$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of dogs to the number of cats (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{50}{30}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of dogs and the denominator represents the number of cats.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{50÷10}{30÷10}=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 4}{3\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $12$ cats in shelter B."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b5e765-8394-5e26-97cb-5181ad7de253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$125$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498960} {:answer/id #uuid "8267c91e-78e7-54f1-810d-56e688dacbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$180$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499022} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$150$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499138} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa9376f-970b-5851-b63a-06d19f7a9bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$160$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499228} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0b57ff-09b4-5306-9f7f-2157afda7e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$130$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$150$ boys" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499138} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7abed6-6b73-5db6-ab00-05e20862640c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ec248fa-4181-5322-854b-62b56bba8e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60072" :question/problem "The following table shows the number of babies born at a hospital in New York during a particular month:\n\n| Boys | Girls |\n| --- | --- |\n| $102$ | $81$ |\n\nApproximately $120$ girls were born at a hospital in Boston during the same month. The ratio of boys to girls was the same at both hospitals. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of boys born at the Boston hospital during that month." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of babies born in the New York Hospital to the nearest $10$:\n\n- Boys: $102⟶100$\n\n- Girls: $81⟶80$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100}{80}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of boys and the denominator represents the number of girls.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100÷10}{80÷10}=\\frac{10}{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $120$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $30$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 30}{4\\times 30}=\\frac{150}{120}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $150$ boys were born at Boston Hospital in that particular month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499441 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71ff81f-388d-53c8-853e-c60430327148" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating Ratios by Rounding to the Nearest Hundred"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d44b2c-7f46-5763-94a1-bf4f8891647f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498887} {:answer/id #uuid "693daa38-3e49-587a-b9f1-8ece9b7b15ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498969} {:answer/id #uuid "deb830c9-bdf2-5924-b45c-bf8c221b5a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499225} {:answer/id #uuid "e12db9f4-426d-50c6-ad4d-5f29c41b8f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499234} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5df837-22b0-59c0-8ce1-0784e2b5404b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d44b2c-7f46-5763-94a1-bf4f8891647f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498887} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b993e3-c224-5545-b5e6-d24529a54d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "842009cb-80b4-53ea-a070-3fcd9cc4ab48" :question/math-academy-id "q-92858" :question/problem "The following table shows the weight, in kilograms, of sand and crushed stone in a concrete mix.\n\n| Sand | Crushed stone |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1\\,224$ | $1\\,645$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the weight of sand and crushed stone by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- sand: $1\\,224⟶1\\,200$\n\n- crushed stone: $1\\,645⟶1\\,600$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,200}{1\\,600}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,200÷100}{1\\,600÷100}=\\frac{12}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷4}{16÷4}=\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone is approximately $\\frac{3}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f8dab9-a608-5cd8-9379-13466349cb11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$52$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498734} {:answer/id #uuid "28615b6e-6fc5-5804-9afc-6daf868b4ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$48$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498817} {:answer/id #uuid "553bf0cf-1717-5c73-8656-42c8cfbe753c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498925} {:answer/id #uuid "bf27713d-59bd-56e8-bb75-d1acd34b7f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$35$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499152} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499265} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9b0300d-ca77-5e40-9b4f-6ccf069cb4cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b402cb00-d472-5e9f-9484-7067afb16406" :question/math-academy-id "q-93275" :question/problem "The building model has the same ratio of length to width as a real building\nThe following table shows the length and width of the building model in centimeters. \n\n| Length | Width |\n| --- | --- |\n| $84$ | $41$ |\n\nBy rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the length of the building if it is known that its width is $20$ meters." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the length and width of the building model:\n\n- Length: $84⟶80$\n\n- Width: $41⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the length to the width (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{80}{40}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the length of the building model, and the denominator represents the width.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{80÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷4}{4÷4}=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $20$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 20}{1\\times 20}=\\frac{40}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the building is approximately $40$ meters."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c107044-05cb-5b72-a382-8e1526bcaf66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$130$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498751} {:answer/id #uuid "426954b7-8774-5772-9e32-fda24a883750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$160$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498883} {:answer/id #uuid "9525c376-32d7-5e67-afa0-fc1bb38c14b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$140$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499052} {:answer/id #uuid "b53fa937-0828-5202-94f7-21ca566eeb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$110$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499133} {:answer/id #uuid "f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499287} :answer-field/id #uuid "482050e1-adac-56eb-8be8-fef04face0ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e3b2f10a-1224-55b9-ac80-e23ac5f6c46a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93289" :question/problem "The following table shows Herbert's height and the length of his shadow, in centimeters. \n\n| Height | Shadow |\n| --- | --- |\n| $197$ | $162$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the height of the object to the length of its ​shadow is the same for different objects at the same moment of time. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the length of the shadow cast by Regina at the same time, if her height is $150$ centimeters." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round Herbert's height and the length of his shadow:\n\n- Height: $197⟶200$\n\n- Shadow: $162⟶160$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the height to the length of the ​shadow (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{200}{160}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the height and the denominator represents the length of the ​shadow.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{200÷10}{160÷10}=\\frac{20}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20÷4}{16÷4}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $150$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $30$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 30}{4\\times 30}=\\frac{150}{120}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the shadow cast by Regina is approximately $120$ centimeters."}]}
